{"id":"word:hebrew:H6726","type":"word","title":"צִיּוֹן","subtitle":"H6726 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Tsijon (as a permanent capital ), a mountain of Jerusalem","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to צִיּוֹן (H6726) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-loc.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 153 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"צִיּוֹן (Tsîyôwn) means Tsijon (as a permanent capital ), a mountain of Jerusalem First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 5."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"צִיּוֹן","transliteration":"Tsîyôwn","pronunciation":"tsee-yone'","strong":"H6726","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6726","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-loc","forms":["צִיּ֔וֹן","צִיּֽוֹן","צִיּ֑וֹן","צִיּ֖וֹן","צִיּ֗וֹן"],"morphs":[["HNp",106],["HR/Np",43],["HC/R/Np",3],["HNp/Sd",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Tsijon (as a permanent capital ), a mountain of Jerusalem","usage":"Zion.","full":"H6726. Tsiyyon צִיּוֺן 154 proper name, of a location Σ ( ε ) ιων ; ‚îyyôn , Zion (Syriac , older form, according to Lag Bn 84 , compare 198); — ׳צ 2Sam 5:7 +; צִיּוֺ֫נָה Jer 4:6 ; &#8212; stronghold (of Jebusiteas), צ ׳מְצֻדַת captured by David, and made his residence 2Sam 5:7 = 1Chr 11:5 (both + דָּוִד עִיר הִיא ), on southern part of east hill of Jerusalem, distinct from site of temple 1Kin 8:1 2Chr 5:2 (both ד ׳מֵעִיר צ ׳הִיא ), not elsewhere in narrative, but often in poets and prophets: as name of Jerusalem, from political point of view (sometimes = inhabitants), Amos 6:7 (|| הַרשֹֿׁמְרוֺן ), || יְרוּשָׁלַםִ Micah 3:10 , 12 = Jer 26:18 ; Isa 4:3 ; 30:19 ; 40:9 ; 41:27 ; 52:1 ; 62:1 ; 64:9 ; Zeph 3:16 ; Zech 1:14 , 17 ; Psalm 51:20 and ( ׳בַּתצֿ ) Isa 52:2 ; Micah 4:8 (|| ׳בַּתיְֿרוּשׁ ), Lam 2:13 (|| id. ), also ( צ ׳יוֺשֶׁבֶת ) Jer 51:35 ; = Jerusalem also Isa 14:32 ; 33:5 +, so especially in phrase צ ׳בְּנוֺת 3:16-17 , 4:4 ; Song 3:11 , צ ׳בְּנֵי Lam 4:2 ; Joel 2:23 ; Psa 149:2 (|| יִשְׂרָזֵל ), cf . Zech 9:13 , צ ׳יָלְדָה אֶתבָּֿנֶיהָ Isa 66:8 , and even ׳הַרצֿ 2Kin 19:31 = Isa 37:32 (both || ׳יְרוּשׁ ), 29:8 (|| אַרִיאֵל 29:7 ), Obadiah 17, 21; Psa 48:12 (|| בְּנוֺת יְהוֺדָה 125:1 ; so also צ ׳הַרבַּֿת Isa 16:1 ; and 10:32 Qr (Kt בית ׃ || ׳נִּבְעַתיְֿרוּשׁ ); compare ׳מְרוֺםצֿ Jer 31:12 ; in following ׳הַרצֿ might refer to temple-hill Isa 10:12 (+ ׳יְרוּשׁ ), 31:4 (+ נִּבְעָתָהּ = ׳יְרוּשׁ 31:5 ), Lam 5:18 ; Joel 3:5 (+ ׳יְרוּשׁ ); specifically of Jerusalem as abode of ׳י and place of his worship Amos 1:2 ; Isa 31:9 ; Zech 8:3 ; Micah 4:2 = Isa 2:3 , Joel 4:16; Psa 102:22 ; 135:21 ; 147:12 (all || ׳יְרוּשׁ ), 76:8 (|| שָׁלֵם ); particular of sanctuary 20:3 (|| קֹדֶשׁ ), 14:7 = Psalm 53:7+; of Jerusalem ׳הַרצֿ 48:3 (|| מֶלֶח קִרְיַת רָב֑ ), 78:68 (|| יְהוּדָה שֵׁבֶט ), Isa 24:23 (|| ׳יְרוּשׁ ), etc.; צ ׳הַרֲרֵי in same sence Psa 133:3 ; particularly of sanctuary Isa 4:5 and (|| הַרקָֿדְשִׁי ) Joel 2:1 ; Joel 4:17; צ ׳קָדְשִׁי הַרֿ Psa 2:6 is seat of king. — See also צ ׳ישֶׁבֶת ׳הַהרצֿ, ׳בַּתצֿ, , below בַּת , יָשַׁב הַר, . צָיוֺן see ציה . צִיּוּן see צוה above.","rootNote":"the same (regularly) as 6725 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 5","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 5","1Kgs 8 1","2Chr 5 2","2Kgs 19 21","2Kgs 19 31","2Sam 5 7","Amos 1 2","Amos 6 1"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":153,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 5","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צִיּ֔וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 1","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צִיּֽוֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"2Chr 5 2","book":"2Chr","chapter":5,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צִיּֽוֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 19 21","book":"2Kgs","chapter":19,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צִיּ֔וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 19